From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:47:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: the shader caches on disk are keyed by the
 translator's id

The backend keeps each program's SPIR-V in <cache>/<key>.spv and its
pipelines in pipelines.list. The SPIR-V key was the HLSL text, the stage and
VK_CACHE_VERSION, a constant to bump by hand when the translator's output
changes for the same source; a build whose translator
(rsx_shader_spirv.cpp) or glslang changed without the bump read an older
build's SPIR-V back as its own. Project Pyrrhus (undecuple's Killzone 2
port) lost the holographic sight's reticle and glow that way after an
update (its issue #25, fixed by its patch 6047, MIT); written here from
that report.

The build now takes the translator's id (cmake/RsxSpirvTranslatorId.cmake:
a SHA-256 of rsx_shader_spirv.cpp, rsx_shader_spirv.h and glslang_VERSION,
taken again when either file changes) and rsx_hlsl_to_spirv_id() adds the
glslang version it runs with. The SPIR-V key and the fourth word of
pipelines.list's header hold it (rsx_vk_cache_key.h): another translator
finds none of the older files and starts a new list; two builds of the same
sources share their cache. The id is logged once ("shader cache:
translator ...").
